  <prompt>
    Implement resolveHeaderConfig(manifestJson, formMetadata) returning a fully-resolved
    ResolvedHeaderConfig — a PURE function (no React, no I/O, no Xrm) mirroring the structure and
    test approach of components/DataGrid/configResolution.ts. Tier 1 = valid layoutJson; Tier 2 =
    metadata-derived defaults. Every output field is fully resolved, and span is ALWAYS clamped to
    min(span, columns).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in pure-function design, tiered configuration merging, and
    exhaustive unit testing of resolution logic. Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/configResolution.ts
    exporting resolveHeaderConfig, ResolvedHeaderConfig, ResolvedHeaderField, and the resolver's
    metadata-input interface, exported from the RecordHeader barrel, with an exhaustive unit-test
    suite passing (ADR-038 KEEP category).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The RecordHeader PCF (033) renders whatever this resolver returns. Tier 1 consumes a valid
      layoutJson (guard from 030); Tier 2 derives a useful default from form metadata so the
      control NEVER renders blank on a form with no configuration (FR-04, NFR-10). The proven
      in-repo shape is components/DataGrid/configResolution.ts resolveConfig — a pure function
      over tiers with per-field merge and metadata-derived fallbacks. Design section 5.3 states
      the tier-2 skip list "already matches synthesizeColumnsFromMetadata's skipSet verbatim"
      (configResolution.ts:361-371) — replicating that exact list is load-bearing. The clamp
      (FR-05) exists because FieldGrid does NOT validate span: each cell applies its own
      gridColumn, so a span 3 field in a columns 2 grid silently creates an implicit third grid
      track. Spec: FR-02, FR-04, FR-05.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
