  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">resolveHeaderConfig is PURE: no React, no I/O, no Xrm, no network. The ONLY permitted side effect is console.warn on invalid/absent config (FR-03). It accepts the RAW manifest string (string | undefined), does JSON.parse inside try/catch, applies isValidRecordHeaderConfiguration from task 030, and on ANY failure (malformed JSON, wrong _version, absent/empty property) emits exactly one console.warn and falls through to tier-2 derived defaults. It MUST NOT throw for any input.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Span clamp applies to EVERY resolved field in BOTH tiers: span = min(span, columns). Applies after span defaulting (unspecified span: textarea renderer defaults to columns, every other renderer defaults to 1 — design 5.2). FieldGrid never validates; the resolver is the only guard (FR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Tier-2 derivation (FR-04): primary name field first at span 2, then up to FOUR further non-system fields in FORM ORDER (metadata insertion order), for at most 5 fields total. Skip the primary id attribute plus the IDENTICAL skip list used by synthesizeColumnsFromMetadata at configResolution.ts:361-371: createdon, modifiedon, createdby, modifiedby, ownerid, statecode, statuscode, versionnumber. Replicate the list locally in this file — it is not exported from DataGrid and this task MUST NOT import DataGrid internals.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Per-field merge precedence for every resolved property: config override ?? form-control/metadata value ?? derived fallback. Label: config label ?? metadata displayName/label ?? humanizeLogicalName(name) (implement humanizeLogicalName locally, mirroring configResolution.ts:521 — it is module-private in DataGrid). Required: config required ?? derived from metadata requirement level. ReadOnly: config readOnly ?? false. Title: config title ?? entity display name from metadata ?? humanized entity logical name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Renderer derivation mirrors the STRUCTURE of rendererFromAttributeType (configResolution.ts:197) — a switch on attributeType + format — but emits the header renderer union from task 030: Money to currency; DateTime with format DateOnly to date, otherwise datetime; Picklist/Status/State to optionset; Boolean to boolean; Lookup to lookup; Memo (multiline string) to textarea; Integer/Decimal/Double/BigInt to number; String and everything else to text. Config fields[].renderer overrides derivation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Output is FULLY resolved: every ResolvedHeaderField carries a concrete non-optional name, label, span, renderer, readOnly, required (maxLines may remain optional — it is renderer-specific to textarea; pass the config value through when present). ResolvedHeaderConfig carries concrete title and columns. columns: config value when 2 or 3; ANY other value (absent, 0, 5, string) normalizes to 3 with the rest of the config still honored.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">summaryField passes through AS-IS (string | undefined — config value when present, otherwise undefined). The RECORDSUMMARY_FIELD default and the metadata-existence gate are applied by task 034 at the wiring site, NOT here. Do not import toolbarLaunchDefaults.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Define the resolver's metadata input interface in this file (e.g. HeaderFormMetadata): entity logical name, entity display name, primaryIdAttribute, primaryNameAttribute, and an insertion-ordered attributes record (name to projected attribute: displayName/label, attributeType, format, requiredLevel) — mirroring the EntityMetadata shape resolveConfig consumes. Document that insertion order = form order and callers guarantee it. Keep it decoupled from IDataverseClient so the function stays unit-testable with plain literals.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">resolveHeaderConfig is a pure function — its unit tests are a KEEP category. The test suite must be exhaustive over the acceptance-criteria matrix, mirroring the DataGrid configResolution test approach.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Shared-library code stays React-free here; nothing in this file may reference React or React-18-only APIs.</constraint>
  </constraints>

