  <justification>
    <existing>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/configResolution.ts:244 resolveConfig — the proven tiered resolver, grep-verified closest neighbor; no header-config resolver exists (grep resolveHeaderConfig returns nothing).</existing>
    <extension>No — resolveConfig resolves a different domain object (grid columns/views/behavior from savedquery layoutXml) and is coupled to grid types; the header resolver resolves fields/spans/renderers from a manifest string. The design mirrors its structure and test approach instead of extending it (spec section 11 table).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without one pure resolver: (a) config precedence spreads through the render path untested (spec section 11); (b) a form with no layoutJson renders a blank control, failing FR-04/NFR-10 acceptance ("renders usefully on a form with no layoutJson at all"); (c) with no clamp, a span 3 field in a columns 2 layout silently creates an implicit third grid track because FieldGrid never validates (FR-05 acceptance fails).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

