  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the design section 5.2 Matter example as manifestJson plus matching metadata, tier 1 resolves: fields exactly as configured in order, labels/renderers/required merged per precedence, every span clamped to columns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a span 3 field with columns 2, the resolved span is 2 (clamp), and given a textarea field with no span in a columns 3 layout, the resolved span is 3 (renderer-derived default).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: manifestJson of undefined, '', '{{{', valid JSON with _version '2.0', and valid JSON with fields missing EACH produce exactly one console.warn plus a tier-2 result — and resolveHeaderConfig never throws for any of them (asserted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tier 2: primary name field first at span 2, then up to 4 further fields in metadata insertion order, at most 5 total; primary id, createdon, modifiedon, createdby, modifiedby, ownerid, statecode, statuscode, versionnumber all excluded (each asserted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Renderer derivation unit-tested per type: Money to currency; DateTime+DateOnly to date; DateTime otherwise to datetime; Picklist, Status, State to optionset; Boolean to boolean; Lookup to lookup; Memo to textarea; Integer, Decimal, Double to number; String/unknown to text; and a config renderer override beats derivation.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">columns of 2 and 3 are honored; columns absent, 0, 5, or non-numeric each normalize to 3 while the rest of the config is still applied.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every ResolvedHeaderField in every test result has concrete name, label, span, renderer, readOnly, required (no undefined); resolved title falls back config title, then entity display name, then humanized logical name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">summaryField: present in config passes through verbatim; absent resolves to undefined — no RECORDSUMMARY_FIELD default in this module (grep of the file shows no toolbarLaunchDefaults import).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The module imports nothing from react, @fluentui, DataGrid internals, services, or hooks (verified by reading the import list); shared-library build and full test suite green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec refs: FR-02 (pure, fully resolved), FR-04 (tier-2 defaults), FR-05 (clamp); design 5.2
    (defaults table), 5.3 (tiers + skip list). The resolver is deliberately tier-SHAPED so a
    config-record tier can slot in later without touching renderers (design 5.1 reversibility).
    Task 033 wires it to live form metadata; keep this module testable with plain object literals.

    ── COMPLETION SUMMARY (2026-08-25) ────────────────────────────────────────
    Delivered: components/RecordHeader/configResolution.ts (265 executable lines,
    13 single-purpose functions, 6 exports) + __tests__/configResolution.test.ts
    (192 tests) + barrel exports. 483/483 green across RecordHeader + types;
    tsc --noEmit exit 0; eslint exit 0. Quality gates: code-review (1 finding,
    fixed) + adr-check (0 violations, 0 warnings).

    ESCALATION CHECK (step 1) — NOT fired. The live DataGrid skipSet at
    configResolution.ts:361-371 matches the spec list EXACTLY (primaryIdAttribute
    + createdon/modifiedon/createdby/modifiedby/ownerid/statecode/statuscode/
    versionnumber). Replicated verbatim; DataGrid was not imported.

    THREE JUDGMENT CALLS task 033/034 should know about:

    1. EMPTY / UNUSABLE `fields` FALLS THROUGH TO TIER 2 (beyond the literal
       acceptance list, required by NFR-10). Task 030's guard is deliberately
       shallow — `fields: []` and `fields: [{}]` both pass it. Rendering either
       verbatim yields a BLANK header, which is exactly the failure NFR-10
       forbids. So entry-level validation lives in the resolver: entries with no
       usable string `name` are dropped, and if NOTHING renderable survives the
       field list falls through to tier-2 derivation (still exactly one warn).
       Nuance: a guard-PASSING config keeps its `title` / `columns` /
       `summaryField` even when only its fields fall through — "the rest of the
       config still honored". Partial drops (some entries bad) stay in tier 1
       and warn once.

    2. `String` + `format: 'TextArea'` DERIVES `text`, NOT `textarea`. The
       renderer table was implemented as the closed set the constraints specify
       (Memo ⇒ textarea; String and everything else ⇒ text). A multiline String
       attribute therefore needs an explicit `"renderer": "textarea"` in config.
       Deliberate — widening the set was not in scope. Flag for 033 UAT.

    3. ATTRIBUTE LOOKUP IS OWN-PROPERTY ONLY (`lookupAttribute`). `fields[].name`
       is maker free text; a plain `attributes[name]` read resolves inherited
       Object.prototype members, so `{"name":"toString"}` would hand back a
       truthy function posing as metadata. Found + fixed at code-review; 5 tests
       cover it.

    Contract notes for 033: every ResolvedHeaderField carries concrete name /
    label / span / renderer / readOnly / required — `maxLines` is the ONE
    optional and is OMITTED (never present-and-undefined). `span` is always
    1..columns. `summaryField` passes through as-is (no RECORDSUMMARY_FIELD
    default — that stays task 034's). `requiredLevel` accepts BOTH the Xrm
    form-control vocabulary (none/required/recommended) and the metadata
    vocabulary (None/SystemRequired/ApplicationRequired/Recommended),
    case-insensitively; `recommended` ⇒ false (Dataverse renders + not *).
    `HeaderFormMetadata.attributes` insertion order IS form order — 033 must
    build it by walking the form's control collection in order.

    Step 7 deviation note: no separate notes/*.md was written (orchestrator
    instruction). All three judgment calls are captured in module JSDoc, asserted
    in tests, and recorded here.
  </notes>

